  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Transpiration"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Transpiration is defined as:"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**The** **loss of water vapour from the leaves of plants**"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Water travels from the roots to the leaves in the xylem vessels; when it reaches the cells of the spongy mesophyll layer in the leaves it **evaporates from the surface of the spongy mesophyll cells **into the **air spaces**\n- Water vapour then **diffuses** out of the air spaces into the surrounding environment via the stomata"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/01/Transpiration-in-plants.png",
   "file": "assets/3c007a164e15-transpiration-in-plants.png",
   "alt": "Transpiration in plants, IGCSE & GCSE Biology revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***Transpiration is the loss of water vapour from the leaves of plants due to evaporation from the surfaces of spongy mesophyll cells***"
  }
 ]
